ine's choice was C8, in the top-left, where White's wall was still open. After E6 the game was nearly even again."}, {"turn": 27, "text": "Opus 5.5 played E2, losing another 3.5 points and sliding from +6.1 to +2.6. The engine preferred C8. Black's edge shrank but did not vanish, and the final result of B+2 shows the rest of the game was a quiet endgame."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py and count.py only parse a pasted board and compute group liberties and area counts of the current position, and the cat/tail/cat >> games.md commands read and append game notes; nothing loops over candidate moves or plays out continuations.", "stop": false}}